 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? A sketch is usually shorter and focuses on one story or character, usually standup or improv. A study is a scientific research paper, often quite long and technical. Kind of, though it can be really interesting. It' like solving a huge puzzle, only the picture on the box is invisible. That's a lovely challenge. Start with the big picture, the broad story or idea the study trying to prove. That'll keep you on track. The key questions the study is trying to answer, and how the authors answer them. That'll tell you whether the study is reliable. Enjoy the storm. A clear sky tomorrow is worth it.",
